# superglue Rust conventions

## Tool error policies

Per-tool: `FailFast`, `Skip`, or `Retry` — respect caller configuration in harness and live loops.

## Secrets and cancellation

- API keys via `secrecy` — zeroize on drop.
- Long work must honor `CancellationToken` (cooperative cancel).

## Chat and tools

- OpenAI-shaped types in `chat/`; tool loop in `complete_with_tools`.
- Parallel tool dispatch within a round is intentional — preserve ordering guarantees documented in `_docs/`.

## Errors

- `thiserror` for typed errors at crate boundaries.
- No ad-hoc `reqwest` call sites outside the client module for model APIs.

## Before PR

```bash
cargo fmt
cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings
cargo test
```

## Protobuf / gRPC

- Schema: `proto/superglue.proto` — regenerate when changing RPC surface.
- Feature `grpc` off by default in consumer builds unless needed.
